.TH "INSPEKT\-INDEX" "1" "2026\-04\-16" "Inspekt 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
inspekt\-index \- Index the current page with full semantic structure
and accessible names.
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]inspekt\f[R] \f[B]index\f[R] [\f[I]OPTIONS\f[R]]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Index the current page with full semantic structure and accessible
names.
.PP
Creates a comprehensive Markdown representation of the page including:
.IP \(bu 2
Page landmarks and semantic structure
.IP \(bu 2
All headings with hierarchy
.IP \(bu 2
Main content paragraphs
.IP \(bu 2
Lists and their items
.IP \(bu 2
Interactive elements (links, buttons, form controls) with accessible
names
.IP \(bu 2
Images with alt text
.PP
The indexed page is saved to cache and can be used by the `inspekt ask'
command to answer questions about the page content.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\f[B]\(enno\-cache\f[R]
Don\(cqt save to cache
.TP
\f[B]\-o\f[R], \f[B]\(enoutput\f[R], \f[I]PATH\f[R]
Save to specific file instead of cache
.TP
\f[B]\(enheadless\f[R]
Run in headless Chrome (no browser extension required)
.TP
\f[B]\(enmirror\-session\f[R]
Mirror cookies/storage from live browser (implies \(enheadless)
.TP
\f[B]\(enurl\f[R], \f[I]TEXT\f[R]
URL to index in headless mode
.SH EXAMPLES
.IP
.EX
inspekt index
inspekt index \-\-no\-cache
inspekt index \-o page.md
inspekt index \-\-headless \-\-url https://example.com
.EE
